    "# 05 - Counting Parameters: Deep vs Wide\n",
    "\n",
    "**Section:** ANNs | **Prereqs:** `ANNs/NNClasses.ipynb` | **Next:** `ANNs/IrisANN`\n",
    "\n",
    "'How big is this model?' has an exact answer. For a `Linear(in, out)` layer:\n",
    "\n",
    "    parameters = in * out   (weights)   +   out   (biases)\n",
    "\n",
    "Two networks with the same layer count can differ by orders of magnitude in\n",
    "parameters, and parameters - not layers - drive memory use, overfitting risk,\n",
    "and training time.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Deep vs wide** is a real trade-off, not a ranking: depth composes features\n",
    "(edges -> shapes -> objects), width holds more features per level. The\n",
    "experiment in `ANNs/DepthVsBreadth.ipynb` measures which wins on Iris."
   ]
  },
